   "reasoning_summary": "C8H14O2S2 with DoU 2. The 13C peak at 182.5 (8) is a carboxylic acid; the remaining unsaturation must be a ring, and with two S atoms this points to a cyclic disulfide. The 1H pattern matches alpha-lipoic acid: 3.55 (CH-S), 3.12 (SCH2), 2.44/1.89 (diastereotopic ring CH2), 2.35 (CH2COOH) and 1.66/1.47 (chain CH2). The eight 13C signals (58.9, 42.9, 41.1, 37.2, 36.5, 31.3, 27.0, 182.5) match literature lipoic acid values (56.3, 40.2, 38.5, 34.6, 33.9, 28.7, 24.4, 180) with a consistent ~+2.5 ppm referencing offset. The integrals were not supplied, so the assigned proton counts (13 + COOH) are inferred."
